<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Motivating Example: GD vs. OGD in a Linear Case</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a motivating example, we compare GD and OGD in training a one-layer linear neural network.
The loss function is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(W):=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left\|Wx_{j}-y_{j}\right\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(W):=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left\|Wx_{j}-y_{j}\right\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{(x_{j},y_{j}\right\}_{j=1}^{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{(x_{j},y_{j}\right\}_{j=1}^{J}</annotation></semantics></math> are training data.
For simplicity, assume that <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:=[x_{1},\cdots,x_{J}]\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:=[x_{1},\cdots,x_{J}]\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times J}</annotation></semantics></math> is of full rank, and the loss function has a unique minimizer <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(W_{*})=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(W_{*})=0.</annotation></semantics></math>
The gradient of <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left(Wx_{j}-y_{j}\right)x_{j}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left(Wx_{j}-y_{j}\right)x_{j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left(W-W_{*}\right)x_{j}x_{j}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{J}\left(W-W_{*}\right)x_{j}x_{j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(W-W_{*})XX^{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(W-W_{*})XX^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>
be sequences of iterates generated by GD and OGD respectively, with a learning rate schedule <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\eta_{t}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\eta_{t}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
For GD, it holds that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|W_{t+1}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|W_{t+1}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-\eta_{t}\nabla\!\mathcal{L}\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}\right)-W_{*}\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-\eta_{t}\nabla\!\mathcal{L}\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}\right)-W_{*}\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right)\left(I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}\right)\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right)\left(I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}\right)\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}\right\|_{2}\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}\right\|_{2}\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\cdot\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\cdot\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Frobenius norm.
On the other hand, for OGD, let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})=U_{t}\Sigma_{t}V_{t}^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})=U_{t}\Sigma_{t}V_{t}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">be the reduced SVD for each <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t.</annotation></semantics></math> Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Orth}\left(\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right)=U_{t}V_{t}^{T}=\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\left(V_{t}\Sigma_{t}^{-1}V_{t}^{T}\right)=\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})P_{t}^{-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Orth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Orth}\left(\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right)=U_{t}V_{t}^{T}=\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\left(V_{t}\Sigma_{t}^{-1}V_{t}^{T}\right)=\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})P_{t}^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}:=V_{t}\Sigma_{t}V_{t}^{T}+\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}\right)\right\|_{2}\left(I-V_{t}V_{t}^{T}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}:=V_{t}\Sigma_{t}V_{t}^{T}+\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}\right)\right\|_{2}\left(I-V_{t}V_{t}^{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">is a positive definite matrix.
It follows that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|W_{t+1}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|W_{t+1}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-\eta_{t}\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})P_{t}^{-1}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-\eta_{t}\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})P_{t}^{-1}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right)\left(I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}P_{t}^{-1}\right)\right\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\left(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right)\left(I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}P_{t}^{-1}\right)\right\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}P_{t}^{-1}\right\|_{2}\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|I-\eta_{t}XX^{T}P_{t}^{-1}\right\|_{2}\left\|W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}-W_{*}\right\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> having eigenvalues between the largest and the smallest nonzero singular values of <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By Eq. (<a href="#A1.Ex14" title="In Appendix A Motivating Example: GD vs. OGD in a Linear Case ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the standard GD with a sufficiently small constant learning rate contracts the distance between <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">GD</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny GD}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at a linear rate.
In contrast, by Eq. (<a href="#A1.Ex19" title="In Appendix A Motivating Example: GD vs. OGD in a Linear Case ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), when <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> is large at the start of training, a larger <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> enables faster convergence in OGD.
As <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}})\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> decreases toward zero, however, <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> must be reduced to ensure convergence of <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathsize="0.710em">OGD</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}^{\textrm{\tiny OGD}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As illustrated in Figure <a href="#A1.F3.sf1" title="Figure 3a ‣ Figure 3 ‣ Appendix A Motivating Example: GD vs. OGD in a Linear Case ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3a</span></a>, for OGD with a constant learning rate <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}\equiv\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}\equiv\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, a large <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> initially drives rapid reduction in the training loss but soon leads to plateauing and oscillation, whereas a smaller <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> results in slower convergence but ultimately achieves a lower final loss. Similar behavior is observed when training nonlinear networks (Figure <a href="#A1.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3b ‣ Figure 3 ‣ Appendix A Motivating Example: GD vs. OGD in a Linear Case ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3b</span></a>).
Therefore, a learning rate schedule adaptively tuned to gradient norms is desirable.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.02981v1/pix/linear_lr.png" id="A1.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/170;" width="224" height="170" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>One-layer linear network </figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.02981v1/pix/attention_lr.png" id="A1.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:224/164;" width="224" height="164" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>One-layer attention </figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>GD vs OGD with varied learning rates (lr)</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Useful Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A2.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A2.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\!\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\!\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3 Convergence Analysis ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\Theta^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{L}(\Theta)+\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\Theta^{\prime})\leq\mathcal{L}(\Theta)+\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(s):=\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(s):=\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\Theta^{\prime})-\mathcal{L}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\Theta^{\prime})-\mathcal{L}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}h^{\prime}(s)ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}h^{\prime}(s)ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta)),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta)),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))-\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))-\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))-\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta)\right\|_{*}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\int_{0}^{1}\left\|\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta+s(\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta))-\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta)\right\|_{*}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta),\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|\Theta^{\prime}-\Theta\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For arbitrary nonnegative values, <math id="A2.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{a_{t}\right\}_{t=1}^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{a_{t}\right\}_{t=1}^{T},</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math> it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}a_{\tau}}\leq\ln\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{a_{1}}\right)+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}a_{\tau}}\leq\ln\left(\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{a_{1}}\right)+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">A similar result is shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, Lemma 3.2]</cite>. For completeness, we include the proof here.
Write <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}:=\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}a_{\tau}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}:=\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}a_{\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math> We first show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}\leq\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}\leq\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math> Indeed, by the Mean Value Theorem, there exists <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}\in[S_{t-1},S_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}\in[S_{t-1},S_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>
such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})=\frac{S_{t}-S_{t-1}}{\xi_{t}}=\frac{a_{t}}{\xi_{t}}\geq\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})=\frac{S_{t}-S_{t-1}}{\xi_{t}}=\frac{a_{t}}{\xi_{t}}\geq\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}\leq 1+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\left(\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})\right)=1+\ln(S_{T})-\ln(S_{1})=1+\ln\left(\frac{S_{T}}{a_{1}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{a_{t}}{S_{t}}\leq 1+\sum_{t=2}^{T}\left(\ln(S_{t})-\ln(S_{t-1})\right)=1+\ln(S_{T})-\ln(S_{1})=1+\ln\left(\frac{S_{T}}{a_{1}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly Eq. (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Lemma B.2. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3 Convergence Analysis ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}:=\frac{\min\{\left\|G_{t}\right\|,\gamma\}}{v_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}:=\frac{\min\{\left\|G_{t}\right\|,\gamma\}}{v_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t}[\cdot]:=\mathbb{E}[\cdot|\Theta_{t-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t}[\cdot]:=\mathbb{E}[\cdot|\Theta_{t-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional expectation given the previous iterates
<math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{0},\cdots,\Theta_{t-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{0},\cdots,\Theta_{t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math>
By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmthm1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ AdaGrad Meets Muon: Adaptive Stepsizesfor Orthogonal Updates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t})-\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t})-\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[-\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1}),\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}O_{t}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[-\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1}),\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}O_{t}\right\rangle\right]+\frac{L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[-\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1})-M_{t},\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}O_{t}\right\rangle\right]-\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}\left\|M_{t}\right\|_{*}\right]+\frac{L\epsilon^{2}}{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\alpha_{t}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[-\left\langle\nabla\!\mathcal{L}(\Theta_{t-1})-M_{t},\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}O_{t}\right\rangle\right]-\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\max\left\{\epsilon,\eta\alpha_{t}\right\}\left\|M_{t}\right\|_{*}\right]+\frac{L\epsilon^{2}}{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}L}{2}\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\alpha_{t}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
