<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex98.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\kappa\sqrt{r}}{T^{\frac{1}{4}}}+\frac{L+\Delta}{\sqrt{T}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\kappa\sqrt{r}}{T^{\frac{1}{4}}}+\frac{L+\Delta}{\sqrt{T}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for large <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Alternatively, if the batch size <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}=t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=T^{-\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=T^{-\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=T^{-q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=T^{-q}</annotation></semantics></math> for
arbitrary <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math> then</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

